\section{Text form}{

Every plan has a text form, which is a stable format and is the plan's
identity: two plans are equal exactly when their text forms are equal.
\code{as.character()} returns it and \code{ftfy_plan()} reads it back to the same
plan, so plans can be written to a file and rebuilt.
\itemize{
\item A step is written \verb{action parameter}, for example \verb{encode latin-1}.
\item Steps are joined with \code{" > "}: \verb{encode latin-1 > decode utf-8}.
\item A plan with no steps is written \code{none}. Its text was not changed.
\item A missing plan is \code{NA}. It belongs to a missing string, and is not the
same thing as a plan with no steps.
}
